      <problem>
        <p>Salary Jamal’s boss gives him a 3% raise every year on his birthday. This means that each year, Jamal’s salary is 1.03 times his last year’s salary. If his original salary was $35,000, his salary after 1 year was $$\text{\$}35,000(1.03)$$, after 2 years was $$\text{\$}35,000(1.03)^{2}$$, after 3 years was $$\text{\$}35,000(1.03)^{3}$$, as shown in the table below. What will Jamal’s salary be after 10 years? Simplify the expression, to show Jamal’s salary in dollars.</p>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <row>
              <cell>Year</cell>
              <cell>Salary</cell>
            </row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell>1</cell>
              <cell>$$\text{\$}35,000(1.03)$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>2</cell>
              <cell>$$\text{\$}35,000(1.03)^{2}$$</cell>
            </row>
